{"id": "EUVD-2026-55560", "enisaUuid": "966f77e8-349c-39c4-9f92-fe98c4deffba", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: core: sysfs: add lock to bos_descriptors_read()\n\nAdd a lock to the function bos_descriptors_read().\n\nThis function accesses udev->bos, which could be simultaneously freed in\nusb_reset_and_verify_device(), a function that is commonly called in\ndrivers all over the kernel.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:03:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:09:06", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c07caee449c968842a350bfefa049889923b8240", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/217774e143d7b5a88739193284b6421be3978601", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab82adf5e63b2d89ead7933ab753b9cedbe028e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e0197fbb0eec588795d5431716a244d9ac8fa93"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hh3m-2ww4-7gxq", "CVE-2026-68374"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1499e99f-8b4b-3732-bed1-579ab3779ecc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "12fc84e8c4288cc8ed5f14a35e077130c2cfece2 <c07caee449c968842a350bfefa049889923b8240"}, {"id": "27a1f749-82a6-3715-a461-11008e55b6aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "2af73518-f31f-36a0-b1ab-53e5bd29c0df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "12fc84e8c4288cc8ed5f14a35e077130c2cfece2 <ab82adf5e63b2d89ead7933ab753b9cedbe028e9"}, {"id": "8843bd62-e283-3190-9d64-32327969d5eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "12fc84e8c4288cc8ed5f14a35e077130c2cfece2 <4e0197fbb0eec588795d5431716a244d9ac8fa93"}, {"id": "9429f49c-a008-3f07-b150-f6cf83c269d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9776